WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
A human arm, a bat wing, a whale flipper.

2
00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.090
Three very different jobs.

3
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:10.350
Look under the skin: one
upper bone, two lower bones,

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.310
a group of wrist bones, five digits.

5
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.740
In all three.

6
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.440
Different on the outside.

7
00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.120
Built on the same plan inside.

8
00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:22.060
So when two animals look almost identical,

9
00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:25.990
how can biologists tell whether
they are truly close relatives?

10
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:31.490
In this mission, you'll see why a shared
plan of bones points to a shared ancestor.

11
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:37.450
Then you'll test a bold claim: that
every living thing shares one ancestor.

12
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.960
Your mission: find out how biologists
can tell whether look-alike animals are

13
00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.650
truly close relatives.
